=== -r skips junctions inside the tree
jt/sub/f.txt:needle
rc=0
=== -r follows a junction given as operand
jt/side/g.txt:needle
rc=0
=== -R follows junctions and reports the loop
jt/side/g.txt:needle
jt/sub/f.txt:needle
grep: warning: jt/sub/loop: recursive directory loop
rc=0
=== -R -s silences the loop warning
jt/side/g.txt:needle
jt/sub/f.txt:needle
rc=0
=== --dereference-recursive is -R
jt/sub/f.txt:1
jt/sub/loop/side/g.txt:1
grep: warning: jt/sub/loop/sub: recursive directory loop
=== -r without operand searches .
sub/f.txt:needle
rc=0
=== -R loop through an operand junction
jt/sub/loop/sub/f.txt:needle
jt/sub/loop/sub/loop/side/g.txt:needle
grep: warning: jt/sub/loop/sub/loop/sub: recursive directory loop
